amara-voice-fixes-2026-11-14.diff  (Taisun applies; agents never touch ~/projects/amara-voice)

Applies on top of the live amara_voice.py that already has the speak and dictate patches (15:47 today).
Touches ONLY amara_voice.py. No LaunchAgent change, no new package, no network.

WHAT IT FIXES (decision 0024)
1. Wake chime followed straight away by the end chime. Code reading shows the dictate hook (interruptible) is not on
   the post-wake path: next_request() calls next_utterance() without interruptible, and the hook only returns while
   DICTATE_PENDING is set (only an app dictation request sets it). The path that does fit: after a bare "Amara" the
   wake chime plays blocking, and the mic frames it recorded were never dropped (run_dictation flushes twice; this
   path never did). The chime's own echo then counts as his one request, the "heard" chime fires, Whisper calls it
   noise, and the loop drops to idle. The old log shows the same blips ("ignored after chime", 0.09 to 0.39 s voiced)
   before the patches; 0.36 and 0.39 sit just under the 0.45 s gate. Fix: next_request waits CHIME_TAIL_S (0.25 s),
   flushes the mic, and also needs the follow-up SNR gate (9 dB). It now logs "[request after chime: ...]" or
   "[ignored after chime: ...]" with numbers only, so if it still happens the log shows why.
   Not proven: I could not run her, so this is from the code and the numbers in the log.
2. Filler lines ("On it.", "One sec.", "Checking now.", "One moment."): streaming.py FILLER_TEXTS, played by
   speak_streaming after FILLER_S = 1.5 s. There is no config switch, so this patch turns them off:
   fillers = () unless AMARA_FILLERS=1. Kept: the earcons ("heard" tick, the 6 s thinking pulse, wake, done, error)
   and "Sorry, say that again?". Her real answer may still start with "On it." / "Done." (SPOKEN_STYLE asks for a
   one-line confirmation); that is her answer, not a filler.
3. Voice only while Amara OS is open. Amara OS writes <voice dir>/app_alive = "<pid> <unix ms>" every 5 s. The loop
   ignores everything except an alarm/timer being stopped unless that file is a regular file you own (no symlink, no
   group/other write), under 15 s old, with a live pid. Closed app: no chime, no recording, no Hermes call, within
   15 s. App reopens: works again, no restart. Choice: a ringing alarm/timer still stops with "stop"/"snooze" and
   scheduled timers still ring (that check comes before the gate). Speak and dictate requests keep their own checks.
   Until you ship the Amara OS build that writes the file, this patch makes the wake word do nothing.
   So: ship the new Amara OS FIRST, open it, check that app_alive exists, then apply this.

