  cp amara_voice.py amara_voice.py.bak-2026-11-14b
  patch --dry-run -p1 amara_voice.py < ~/projects/nexus-amara/tasks/proposed/amara-voice-fixes-2026-11-14.diff
  patch -p1 amara_voice.py < ~/projects/nexus-amara/tasks/proposed/amara-voice-fixes-2026-11-14.diff
  (only if the dry run is clean) restart Amara Voice the way you usually do.
  No config edit is needed for the fillers (they are off by default). To get them back, set AMARA_FILLERS=1 in the
  service environment.

TEST STEPS
  1. Amara OS open, wait 10 s, `ls ~/projects/amara-voice/app_alive` exists. Say "Hey Amara": one wake chime, then
     she keeps listening until you stop talking; ask something; no "On it." style line before the answer.
  2. Quit Amara OS, wait 15 s. "Hey Amara": nothing at all (no chime). A timer set earlier still rings.
  3. Reopen Amara OS, wait 10 s. "Hey Amara" works again with no restart.
  4. Still chimes out? Tell me, and send the "[request after chime: ...]" / "[ignored after chime: ...]" numbers.

